  "Notes": "Cavity inducing complete s-polarized absorption in a weak absorber (n0 = 1.4 - i0.04) from a Si hemicylinder by internal reflection\nSpecification: Rs = 0 at alpha = 28.8 deg in the Si hemicylinder, s polarization.\nReported: Table I s design: Rp = 0.989, Rs = 0.001 at alpha = 28.8 deg. Absorber in direct contact with Si (no films): Rp = 0.82, Rs = 0.93 (text p. 2112).\nNotes: Same assumptions as Harrick1970-TableI-p: h/lambda thicknesses scaled with reference_nm = 1000 (0.043 -> 43 nm, 0.260 -> 260 nm); paper's list reversed (FTR film next to the Si hemicylinder). Fig. 5 (p. 2114) uses this s design scaled to 4 um with a gold emitter replacing the absorber (gold index at 4 um not given; not rebuilt).\nLayers from Table I (s design), p. 2112; construction Fig. 1, p. 2111; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours Rp 0.989, Rs 0.011 at 28.8 deg, 1000 nm; paper Rp 0.989, Rs 0.001 (Tables I and III).",
